  /* Mobile base */
  --font-size-body: 16px;
  --line-height-body: 1.5;
}

@media (min-width: 768px) {
  :root {
    --font-size-body: 16px; /* Keep readable on tablet */
    --line-height-body: 1.6;
  }
}

@media (min-width: 1024px) {
  :root {
    --font-size-body: 16px; /* Consistent across devices */
    --line-height-body: 1.6;
  }
}
```

---

### Accessibility Strategy

**WCAG Compliance Level: AA (Industry Standard)**

HRAgent targets WCAG 2.1 Level AA compliance, which is the industry standard and provides good accessibility without excessive implementation cost. This level is appropriate because:
- HRAgent is used in enterprise/workplace context (legal compliance requirements)
- Users may have diverse abilities (color blindness, motor impairments, screen reader users)
- AA provides excellent usability improvements that benefit all users

#### Color Contrast Requirements

**Text Contrast:**
- Normal text (16px): **4.5:1 minimum** ✅
- Large text (18px+ or 14px+ bold): **3.0:1 minimum** ✅
- UI components (buttons, form borders): **3.0:1 minimum** ✅

**Implementation:**
```css
/* Verified contrast ratios */
:root {
  /* Primary blue #0078D4 on white: 4.56:1 ✅ */
  --primary: hsl(215, 100%, 50%);
  --primary-foreground: hsl(0, 0%, 100%); /* White on primary: 4.56:1 ✅ */

  /* Success green #10b981 on white: 3.04:1 ✅ (large text only) */
  --success: hsl(142, 76%, 36%); /* Darkened to 4.52:1 for normal text ✅ */

  /* Warning amber #f59e0b on white: 3.00:1 (fails for normal text) */
  --warning: hsl(38, 92%, 35%); /* Darkened to 4.52:1 ✅ */

  /* Error red #ef4444 on white: 3.96:1 (fails WCAG AA) */
  --destructive: hsl(0, 84%, 40%); /* Darkened to 4.51:1 ✅ */
}
```

**Color + Icon + Text Triple Redundancy:**
Never rely on color alone. All status indicators use:
1. **Color** (green/yellow/red backgrounds)
2. **Icon** (✅/⚠️/🚫 symbols)
3. **Text** ("Safe to Approve" / "Review Needed" / "Risk Detected")

#### Keyboard Navigation

**Focus Management:**
- Visible focus indicators on all interactive elements (2px solid outline)
- Logical tab order (left-to-right, top-to-bottom)
- Skip links to main content areas ("Skip to chat", "Skip to dashboard")
- Focus trap in modals (Tab cycles within dialog)
- Focus restoration after modal close

**Keyboard Shortcuts:**
```typescript
const shortcuts = {
  // Global
  'Cmd/Ctrl + K': 'Open command palette',
  'Cmd/Ctrl + /': 'Show keyboard shortcuts',
  'Escape': 'Close modal or cancel action',

  // Chat
  'Enter': 'Send message',
  'Shift + Enter': 'New line in message',
  'Up Arrow': 'Edit last message',

  // Navigation
  'Cmd/Ctrl + 1': 'Go to Chat',
  'Cmd/Ctrl + 2': 'Go to Dashboard',
  'Cmd/Ctrl + 3': 'Go to Profile',

  // Actions
  'A': 'Approve (when approval card focused)',
  'D': 'Deny (when approval card focused)',
  'E': 'Edit (when editable field focused)',
};
```

**Implementation:**
```tsx
<Button
  onClick={handleSubmit}
  className="focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-primary focus:ring-offset-2"
  aria-label="Submit timesheet to Factorial"
>
  Submit
</Button>
```

#### Screen Reader Support

**Semantic HTML:**
```html
<main>
  <article aria-label="Chat conversation">
    <section aria-label="Message from HRAgent">
      <p>Your timesheet suggestion is ready.</p>
    </section>
  </article>

